.TH CCOL_CHANNEL_DESTROY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
ccol_channel_destroy \- destroy a ccol_channel
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_channel_destroy(ch);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Frees all resources associated with the ccol_channel including both internal
queues. The ccol_channel pointer is automatically set to NULL.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
ch   Channel to destroy (will be set to NULL)
.fi
.SH WARNINGS
.nf
Messages remaining in either direction cause assertion failure
Drain both queues before destroying
A ccol_select()/ccol_select_timed() call or a ccol_event_loop registration
(ccol_selectable_from_chan) still watching either direction also causes
assertion failure; the still-linked waiter would otherwise reference
the underlying queue's own, about-to-be-freed mutex
Call ccol_event_loop_remove(), or let every watching ccol_select()/
ccol_select_timed() call return, before destroying
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Safe to call with NULL pointer
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_channel_create (3),
.BR __ccol_channel_destroy (3)
